WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.101 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-How are you, my friend?

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.002 line:92%
-This feels -- It feels great.

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:04.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is very --
It's surreal to introduce you.

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:05.105 line:92%
-I don't know how to sit.

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:07.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We've known each other --
Right, you don't know.

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:08.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know this side.
Yeah, exactly.

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:10.610 size:78% position:39%
We probably have more
in common than two --

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.947
than any other human beings
on the face of the Earth.

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:14.381 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:16.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We both were on
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:16.750 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yep.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:17.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We both did Weekend Update.
-We did.

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:19.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We both hosted "Late Night."
-Yeah.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:22.489
-We both have two babies.
-We both have two babies.

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:23.289 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:26.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We are mirror --
-We are mirror images.

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I want to say
that introducing you

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
is such a nice thing for me
to be able to do

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:33.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you introduced me
the very first time

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.535 size:81% position:41%
I did Weekend Update
when you were hosting.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:36.102 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's right.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:39.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is 2001 -- this was like
October probably of 2001.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:43.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we have the clip because
you and I look different.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:47.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is just Jimmy
introducing me in 2001.

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:49.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What does my hair look like?
Oh, no.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:51.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, a tough night
for the New York Yankees.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:55.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
They lost to Arizona, 15-2.
[ Audience awws ]

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.724 size:78% position:39%
The series is tied at
three games apiece.

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:00.994 size:88% position:44%
Here with the commentary
is our own Seth Meyers.

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:01.761 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thanks, Jimmy.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:06.499 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think we look exactly
the same.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:09.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We look exactly --
-Exactly.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:10.737 line:92%
What was I doing with that?

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:13.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was in -- I felt like I was
in a caveman phase.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.908 line:92%
-Also, our suits were worse.

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:17.610 size:81% position:41%
-I never owned a suit
before Weekend Update.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.880 size:88% position:44%
-That was the first time
you ever had a jacket?

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:21.614 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Yeah, it really was.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:24.651
Lorne was like, "You need a suit
and tie for Update."

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:27.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "I don't know what
that means.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
A clip-on?
Can I use a clip-on?"

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.790 line:92%
I mean, so many good memories.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you miss it?
Do you still miss "SNL"?

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know now you're kind of
two shows past it

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:36.963
'cause "Late Night," now you're
doing "The Tonight Show."

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:39.666
-Yeah. I do -- Every now and
then you miss the excitement

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the feeling of
the last-minute sketch

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:43.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you don't know it's going
to get written or whatever.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:46.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you remember
when Mick Jagger hosted?

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:46.506 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I do.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:47.907
-We were all nervous
because it was like Lorne said,

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.009
"Mick said he'll do something."
-Yeah.

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:50.643 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-And I go, "Okay."

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.378 size:81% position:41%
And everyone is just
afraid of Mick Jagger,

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:53.313 line:92%
so no one pitched him anything.

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:55.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like, "We should pitch
him an idea."

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:56.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I go,
"I'll pitch him something."

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:59.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "What if I'm
his reflection in the mirror?"

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:00.053 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I'm like...

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:03.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Speaking gibberish
as Mick Jagger ]

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:06.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Lorne goes,
"Please don't do that."

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:06.993 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Don't do that.
It's insulting to Mick.

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:10.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the bit has been done
in the mirror.

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:13.066 size:75% position:38%
Groucho Marx did it.
Lucille Ball did it.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:15.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're not gonna
break any ground with this."

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:18.471
I go, "Okay, that's fine.
I'll come up with an idea."

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:19.305 line:92%
So I go and write the sketch,

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then they go, "You have to
go pitch it to Mick."

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:23.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "I don't want to
talk to Mick."

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:24.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, he's -
It's Mick Jagger.

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:26.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I went in,
and he's so cool-looking.

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:27.514 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's Mick Jagger.

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:29.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's like, "Lovely to meet
you, hello."

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:32.619
And I go, "I have ideas.
My name is Jimmy Fallon."

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:33.319 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I pitched him my idea.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "It's me and you
working at a mall."

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:38.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
He goes, "No.
I don't like that."

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:38.758 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:39.292 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I go, "Oh, okay.

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:41.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
Here's one where we're
the Rolling Stones,

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:43.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we're like a wedding band
Rolling Stones."

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Uh, no, not really my thing."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:49.235
I go, "How about an idea of --"
He doesn't like anything.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:49.736 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So I leave.

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "He doesn't
like anything."

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:52.071 size:75% position:38% line:92%
So then it's Friday,

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:54.774
which usually the sketches have
to be written on Tuesday.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:55.575 line:92%
It's Friday and Lorne goes,

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:59.212
"Mick's still up to do something
if you have any more ideas."

00:02:59.212 --> 00:02:59.746 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I go, "Okay."

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:01.714
So I came up with ideas.
I went back and he looks at me.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like, "You again."
And I go, "Hi. I have an idea.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe I'm --
you're Keith and I'm Keith

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:09.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's cloned himself
so he can party with himself."

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:10.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
He goes,
"No, I don't like that."

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:11.758 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:13.693 line:92%
So I go, "What if it's you --

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:17.564
you're hosting the show and I'm
your reflection in the mirror.

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:18.665 line:92%
And I'm going like that..."

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:21.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he goes,
"I love it! That's great."

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:22.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, my gosh.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:23.436 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Dude, good news is --

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:26.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it's very --
it's a very iconic sketch.

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:27.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
There it is.
Look at you guys.

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:28.942 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:29.909 line:92%
-Good news is, he loves it.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
Bad news is
it's the mirror sketch.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:32.979 line:92%
-And you had to go tell Lorne.

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had to give him
the bad news.

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:35.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Of course.
Yeah, the bad.

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:38.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "He wants to do it,
but it's the mirror sketch."

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:40.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You -- I mean, it was
my first year.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:42.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
You'd had been on the show
a few years.

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:43.156 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I remember you, Horatio

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:44.691 size:75% position:38%
were very nice to me
in the early days.

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:48.127
And I remember thinking, "Oh,
if I hang out with those guys,

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:49.295 line:92%
I'm going to meet famous people.

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll go out drinking with
famous people."

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:54.067
And I would say the one -- the
person we went out drinking with

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:57.303
who was the most fun was famous,
but not the kind of like --

00:03:57.303 --> 00:04:00.073 size:75% position:38%
I was hoping to meet
Hollywood starlets.

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:00.573 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:03.109
-And instead, we went out
drinking with David Wells.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:03.876 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:05.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. That is true.
-Yeah.

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:07.680 size:81% position:41%
-Yeah, no, Wellsy --
yes, the great pitcher

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.182 line:92%
for the New York Yankees.

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:09.616 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:10.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In fact,
do you remember the story?

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:13.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which one?
-The one. The one and only.

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:14.087 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Which was the one?

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.321 line:92%
-The one and only is this one.

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:17.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know,
we had a lot of good ones.

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:18.057 size:78% position:39% line:92%
But he's a great guy.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:20.326
No, this is -- gosh, we can't do
this anymore.

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:21.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we were at
the "SNL" after party

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:26.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
with you, Horatio,
Lorne, and David Wells.

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:29.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's probably 5:30
in the morning.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:29.869 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:32.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I'm -- I go, "I've got to
go home, man.

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:34.040 line:92%
I'm just exhausted, man."

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.441 size:75% position:38% line:92%
We had a few drinks.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:36.175 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:36.843 size:75% position:38% line:92%
5:30 in the morning.

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:39.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or Lorne left at like 4:00 or
something like that,

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:43.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
but then we stayed until 5:30,
I want to say, 5:00.

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:44.017 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I left and went home.

00:04:44.017 --> 00:04:46.886
Woke up the next day around 1:30
in the afternoon.

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:49.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
I turn on the TV
and it's the Yankees game,

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:51.357 line:92%
and David Wells is pitching.

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:51.891 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:54.861
-So I go, "It's got to be one of
those classic games."

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:55.428 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, classic.

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:57.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, classic,
where they replay the game.

00:04:57.163 --> 00:05:00.300
I go, "That's pretty funny
'cause I was just with him."

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.802
And it's not, it's a real game.
-Yeah.

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:03.503 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-So I call up Horatio.

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:06.906
I go, "Dude --" and I wake him
up at 2:00 in the afternoon.

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:08.174 line:92%
I go, "Dude, turn on channel 11.

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:10.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Yank-- David Wells is
pitching right now.

00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:13.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like, "Wells?
There's no way."

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:13.746 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I go, "I know.

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:16.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
He goes, "We left him.
It was 5:30."

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:17.517 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I go, "I know, dude."

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:19.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he turned it on.
It was pitching.

00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:23.056
And that was the game he pitched
the perfect game.

00:05:23.056 --> 00:05:25.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:26.125 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's insane!

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:30.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's because of me
he was that calm!

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.565 size:81% position:41% line:92%
He owes me everything.

